{%- comment -%}
  product-giveaway
  ----------------
  Standalone product template section for the free 5ml claim page.

  LAYOUT — ONE COLUMN, BUILT TO JEFF'S WIREFRAME (docs/giveaway-qa/jeff-wireframe.jpg).
  A single centred card, same at every width, in this exact order:
    1. hero photo (`hero_image`, falling back to the product image)
    2. dark PILL eyebrow — "One-time free product giveaway"
    3. HEADLINE, two lines, built from live values: the shipping charge and the
       product title. "Pay $4.99 for shipping, / get <product> for free."
    4. the FTC conditions list  <- see the adjacency note below
    5. the SUBSCRIBE & SAVE module — the paid option, offered before the claim
    6. the CLAIM button
    7. fineprint, which SWITCHES when a subscription has been chosen
  Two earlier revisions (two peer cards side by side; then a quiet text strip)
  were both rejected. If you are tempted to reinstate either, that is the history.
  Everything still lives inside #bnGiveChoice, which is the element the
  IntersectionObserver watches, so the sticky bar cannot cover the claim button.

  WHY THE CONDITIONS SIT ABOVE THE SUBSCRIBE MODULE AND NOT BELOW IT.
  The wireframe puts the module directly under the headline. The conditions were
  placed between them instead, deliberately: the module is a DIFFERENT offer at a
  DIFFERENT price, and interposing it between the word "free" and the conditions
  attached to that word is exactly the separation 16 CFR 251.1(c)(1) is about.
  Conditions first, then the second offer. Do not reorder these two.

  THE THREE CLICKS. Choose (a scent) -> Claim (the free bottle) -> Checkout.
  The subscription is added to the cart the moment a scent is chosen, NOT at
  claim time, so the claim button keeps its single job and its existing guards.

  FREE SHIPPING ON THE SUBSCRIPTION IS A PROMISE THIS THEME CANNOT KEEP ON ITS OWN.
  The module says "+ free shipping" and the fineprint says the shipping charge is
  waived. Nothing in Liquid makes that true — it depends on an AUTOMATIC discount
  configured in Shopify admin (Discounts > Create > Amount off delivery >
  Automatic, minimum subtotal $10, all countries the store ships to). If that
  discount does not exist, the customer is charged shipping and the page has lied.
  `sub_free_shipping` (checkbox, default true) is the switch: turn it OFF and
  every free-shipping word disappears from the module and the fineprint, and the
  fineprint states the shipping charge instead. Turn it off if the discount is
  ever paused, expired, or scoped away from this product.

  MIXED CART (free $0 bottle + a subscription line). Verified against the cart
  surfaces on this branch, no changes were needed:
    - templates/cart.liquid keeps `has_subscription` TRUE whenever any line
      carries a selling plan, so the ROSCA disclosure and its consent checkbox
      both render, and checkout stays gated on the checkbox.
    - Both cart.liquid and snippets/cart-drawer.liquid already refuse to assert
      "Shipping FREE" when a giveaway line is present and print "Calculated at
      checkout" instead. The free-shipping discount is applied by Shopify at
      checkout, not asserted by the theme.
    - Neither surface gives the giveaway line a working quantity stepper.

  WHY THIS EXISTS (do not "simplify" this back onto main-product):
  `sections/main-product.liquid` contains the Bug D guard — any product with
  `product.selling_plan_groups.size == 0` renders a permanently DISABLED
  "Subscription unavailable" button. A $0 one-time SKU is exactly that product,
  so it is unbuyable on the default product template. This section routes around
  the guard rather than weakening it. It deliberately contains NO Appstle widget,
  NO swap modal, NO "Queue for a Future Month" button and NO selling_plan input.

  WHY NO SELLING PLAN IS ATTACHED TO *THIS* PRODUCT: Appstle derives the
  recurring charge from the product price, so a $0 product would recur at $0.
  The Subscribe & Save module never puts a plan on the giveaway SKU — it adds a
  SEPARATE line for a real fragrance, at that fragrance's own price and plan.

  WHY THE MODULE USES window.__bnFetch AND THEN RE-READS /cart.js:
  Appstle's wrapper around window.fetch STRIPS `selling_plan` from add payloads
  (store-wide incident, Jul 16-17 2026), which converts a subscription into a
  silent one-time full-price line. layout/theme.liquid captures a pristine fetch
  as window.__bnFetch before any app script loads. Capturing it is not enough on
  its own: /cart/add.js can return a line WITHOUT selling_plan_allocation even
  when the plan did apply, so the module re-reads /cart.js and, if the plan is
  genuinely missing, REMOVES the line rather than leaving a full-price surprise.

  COMPLIANCE NOTES (do not move these strings below the fold or into the FAQ):
  - 16 CFR 251.1(c)(1): every condition on a "Free" offer must be disclosed
    clearly and conspicuously AT THE OUTSET. Footnotes and asterisks are
    expressly rejected. The shipping charge, one-per-customer limit and US-only
    limit therefore live INSIDE the same block as the word Free.
    ONE STATEMENT, NOT FOUR (dedupe pass, Aug 2026): the conditions now appear
    exactly once per surface, in `.bn-give__terms`, immediately under the word
    Free. The old repeats — the "+ $X shipping" chip on the price line, the
    "Bottle $0 · Shipping $X" box, and the shipping charge appended to the
    button label — were removed as duplication, NOT as disclosure. The terms
    list is now the whole disclosure for this surface: if you delete a line from
    it, the condition is no longer disclosed anywhere on the card.
    This obligation applies to EVERY restatement of the claim, not just the
    first one: the sticky mobile bar repeats "Free" after the hero has scrolled
    away, so it carries its own single conditions line. Any new surface that
    says "free" — badge, banner, drawer, email — inherits the same obligation.
  - 16 CFR 233.1: no compare-at / strikethrough price. This SKU has never been
    sold standalone, so any "was" price would be fictitious.
  - 16 CFR 435 (Mail Order Rule): the ship commitment is stated separately from
    the transit time.
  - Language: this is a sale, not a lottery. Never use win / winner / enter /
    entry / drawing / lucky / sweepstakes anywhere in customer-facing copy.
    Use "claim".

  `show_cap` (checkbox, DEFAULT OFF) — batch cap and stock chip.
  Jeff pulled the "40 bottles" framing off the page. With `show_cap` off, NO
  cap-derived and NO inventory-derived string renders anywhere: not the terms
  bullet, not the scarcity chip, not the sticky bar clause, and the sold-out
  headline falls back to the neutral "This release is finished" instead of
  "All 40 bottles are gone." Turning it back on restores all four at once and
  re-arms the `cap_trusted` guard described below. The sold-out LOGIC is
  independent of this switch and keeps working either way — it is driven by
  `product.available`, never by the typed cap.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign current_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign featured_image = current_variant.featured_image | default: product.featured_image

  assign show_cap = section.settings.show_cap
  assign cap = section.settings.cap | default: 40
  assign ship_amount = section.settings.ship_amount | default: '$4.99'
  assign claim_label = section.settings.claim_label | default: 'Claim my free bottle'
  assign claim_label_short = section.settings.claim_label_short | default: 'Claim my free bottle'

  comment
    Guards the word "free" in the headline against a SKU that is not actually
    $0. Never assume the price: `| money` renders "$0.00" either way.
  endcomment
  assign price_is_zero = false
  if current_variant.price == 0
    assign price_is_zero = true
  endif
  comment
    Off by default: the page opens on the photo. It has no schema default (a
    blank schema default is rejected by the Shopify server), so it renders only
    when someone types something into it.
  endcomment
  assign choice_intro = section.settings.choice_intro

  comment
    Prices are section settings so this page can be priced independently of the
    storefront default, and they fall back to the global theme settings the
    subscription-renewal-disclosure snippet reads, so the two can never contradict
    each other when the section fields are cleared.
  endcomment
  assign sub_price = section.settings.sub_price | default: settings.subscription_price | default: '$20/month'
  assign sub_first_price = section.settings.sub_first_price | default: settings.subscription_first_order_price | default: '$15'

  assign option_b_url = section.settings.option_b_url | default: '/collections/all'
  if section.settings.option_b_product != blank
    assign option_b_url = section.settings.option_b_product.url
  endif

  assign sub_free_shipping = section.settings.sub_free_shipping
  assign picker_title = section.settings.picker_title | default: 'Choose your second scent'
  assign picker_explore_label = section.settings.picker_explore_label | default: 'Explore this scent'

  comment
    HEADLINE. Two lines, each interpolated from live values so the shipping
    charge and the product name can never drift from the rest of the page:
      {ship}       -> the Shipping charge setting
      {product}    -> product.title
      {sub_first}  -> first month price      {sub_price} -> price after that
    The injected values are escaped; the merchant's own sentence around them is
    printed as typed, the same as every other text setting in this section.
  endcomment
  assign t_ship = ship_amount | escape
  assign t_product = product.title | escape
  assign t_sub_first = sub_first_price | escape
  assign t_sub_price = sub_price | escape

  assign headline_line1 = section.settings.headline_line1 | default: 'Pay {ship} for shipping,'
  assign headline_line1 = headline_line1 | replace: '{ship}', t_ship | replace: '{product}', t_product | replace: '{sub_first_price}', t_sub_first | replace: '{sub_first}', t_sub_first | replace: '{sub_price}', t_sub_price

  assign headline_line2 = section.settings.headline_line2 | default: 'get {product} for free'
  assign headline_line2 = headline_line2 | replace: '{ship}', t_ship | replace: '{product}', t_product | replace: '{sub_first_price}', t_sub_first | replace: '{sub_first}', t_sub_first | replace: '{sub_price}', t_sub_price

  assign fineprint = section.settings.fineprint | default: 'Pay only shipping today. No subscription, no auto-renewal.'
  assign fineprint = fineprint | replace: '{ship}', t_ship | replace: '{product}', t_product | replace: '{sub_first_price}', t_sub_first | replace: '{sub_first}', t_sub_first | replace: '{sub_price}', t_sub_price

  comment
    The subscribed fineprint carries NO schema default on purpose (same pattern
    as faq_a1 below): a schema default would freeze the wording and, worse,
    would keep promising waived shipping after `sub_free_shipping` is switched
    off. Generated, it follows the switch automatically.
  endcomment
  assign fineprint_sub = section.settings.fineprint_sub
  if fineprint_sub == blank
    if sub_free_shipping
      assign fineprint_sub = 'Today: ' | append: ship_amount | append: ' shipping is waived; your card is charged ' | append: sub_first_price | append: ' today, then ' | append: sub_price | append: ' until you cancel.'
    else
      assign fineprint_sub = 'Today: ' | append: ship_amount | append: ' shipping, plus ' | append: sub_first_price | append: ' for your first month; then ' | append: sub_price | append: ' until you cancel.'
    endif
  else
    assign fineprint_sub = fineprint_sub | replace: '{ship}', t_ship | replace: '{product}', t_product | replace: '{sub_first_price}', t_sub_first | replace: '{sub_first}', t_sub_first | replace: '{sub_price}', t_sub_price
  endif

  comment
    PICKER SOURCE. `fragrances` is the handle the rest of the theme already uses
    (templates/product.json wires a related-products section to it). It is read
    through a setting first so the campaign can be pointed somewhere else without
    a code change, and it falls back to `all` rather than rendering an empty
    modal — an empty picker behind a "Choose" button is a dead end, not a
    graceful degradation. Products with no selling plan, and this giveaway SKU
    itself, are skipped at render time.
  endcomment
  assign pick_collection = section.settings.picker_collection
  if pick_collection == blank
    assign pick_collection = collections['fragrances']
  endif
  assign pick_products = pick_collection.products
  if pick_products.size == 0
    assign pick_products = collections['all'].products
  endif

  comment
    Does the picker have anything to offer? Counted BEFORE render so the module
    can degrade to a plain link instead of opening an empty sheet.
  endcomment
  assign pick_count = 0
  for p in pick_products limit: 60
    if p.handle != product.handle and p.selling_plan_groups.size > 0
      assign pick_count = pick_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Is a subscription ALREADY in this cart? Rendered server-side so a reload
    shows the chosen state and, critically, so the recurring-charge disclosure
    is present on first paint whenever a recurring line genuinely exists —
    rather than depending on JS having run. sessionStorage is a convenience on
    top of this, never the source of truth.
  endcomment
  assign cart_sub_line = blank
  for line in cart.items
    if line.selling_plan_allocation
      assign cart_sub_line = line
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Hero image. Jeff's shot is the full bottle next to the Base Note 5 ml
    atomizer, so it is a wide image at the top of the free card, not the 88px
    thumbnail this section used to carry. Falls back to the product image, and
    when it does, the alt text falls back with it — a generic product shot must
    not inherit alt text describing a photo that is not on screen.
  endcomment
  assign hero_img = section.settings.hero_image | default: featured_image
  assign hero_alt = section.settings.hero_image_alt | default: 'Mont Blanc Legend next to a Base Note 5 ml atomizer'
  if section.settings.hero_image == blank
    assign hero_alt = featured_image.alt | default: product.title
  endif

  comment
    Scarcity is SERVER-RENDERED from real inventory and reported as a band,
    never as a live decrementing JS counter. If inventory is untracked we fall
    back to the release statement, which is a business fact we can stand behind.

    `cap` is a hand-typed number in the theme editor and is NOT wired to real
    inventory. If the two disagree — more bottles in stock than the merchant
    typed — every cap-derived string becomes false ("52 of 40 left", "40 bottles
    in this batch" while 52 exist). `cap_trusted` is the guard: when real
    inventory exceeds the typed cap we print NO cap line and NO scarcity band at
    all, rather than printing a number we cannot stand behind. A suppressed
    condition is safe under 16 CFR 251.1 in a way that a false one is not.
    `show_cap` sits IN FRONT of that guard: off, and nothing cap-derived is even
    computed.
  endcomment
  assign qty = current_variant.inventory_quantity

  assign cap_trusted = false
  if show_cap
    assign cap_trusted = true
    if qty > cap
      assign cap_trusted = false
    endif
  endif

  assign scarcity_line = ''
  if cap_trusted
    assign release_line = cap | append: ' bottles in this batch'
    if current_variant.inventory_management == blank
      assign scarcity_line = release_line
    elsif qty > 25
      assign scarcity_line = release_line
    elsif qty > 8
      assign scarcity_line = qty | append: ' of ' | append: cap | append: ' left'
    elsif qty > 0
      assign scarcity_line = 'Only ' | append: qty | append: ' left'
    endif
  endif

  comment
    ONCE PER CUSTOMER (Jeff: "customers can only do it once"). Two layers,
    because neither one covers the other's case:

      1. CART layer — `already_claimed`. Stops a second bottle inside one
         session. /cart/add.js MERGES a matching line and ADDS the quantity, so
         without this, a reload plus a second press is all it takes to hold two
         against a disclosed "one per customer" condition.
      2. CUSTOMER layer — `customer_claimed`. Stops a logged-in customer who
         already ORDERED from claiming again later, on any device. A theme
         cannot query order history, so this reads a customer tag written by
         Shopify Flow.

    Build BOTH workflows in Shopify admin > Flow. The product handle is printed
    on the section root as `data-bn-give-handle` so it can be copied straight
    off the rendered page into the Flow condition:

      FLOW 1 — tag the claimer
        Trigger:   Order created
        Condition: Order / Line items / any / Product / Handle  equals  <handle>
        Action:    Add customer tags  ->  giveaway_claimed

      FLOW 2 — catch the repeat claim
        Trigger:   Order created
        Condition: Order / Line items / any / Product / Handle  equals  <handle>
                   AND Order / Customer / Tags  contains  giveaway_claimed
        Action:    Cancel order (refund, restock)
                   Send internal email  ->  the team address

    Keep them as TWO separate workflows. Flow 2's condition reads the customer
    as they were before this order was tagged, which is what makes it fire on
    the second order and not the first; merged into one workflow the ordering of
    the tag action and the tag condition is undefined.

    A logged-OUT repeat claimer still reaches checkout. That is deliberate:
    Flow 2 reverses it after the fact, and forcing account creation before a
    free bottle would cost more real claims than it saves.
  endcomment
  assign already_claimed = false
  for line in cart.items
    if line.properties['_bn_offer'] == 'free-5ml'
      assign already_claimed = true
    endif
  endfor

  assign customer_claimed = false
  if customer and customer.tags contains 'giveaway_claimed'
    assign customer_claimed = true
  endif

  assign show_claim = true
  if customer_claimed or already_claimed
    assign show_claim = false
  endif

  comment
    FAQ answer 1 quotes the shipping charge, so it is built here from
    `ship_amount` instead of being hardcoded. `faq_a1` deliberately carries NO
    schema default — a schema default would win over this interpolated string
    and re-freeze the figure at whatever was typed into the schema.
  endcomment
  assign ship_amount_html = ship_amount | escape
  assign faq_a1_default = '<p>Yes. The bottle itself costs $0. You pay ' | append: ship_amount_html | append: ' for flat-rate tracked shipping, plus sales tax on that shipping charge in states that tax it, which is why your total may not be exactly ' | append: ship_amount_html | append: '. There is no trial and no second charge.</p>'
-%}

<div class="bn-give" id="bnGiveRoot" data-bn-give-handle="{{ product.handle }}">
  <div class="bn-give__wrap">

    {%- if choice_intro != blank -%}
      <p class="bn-give__intro">{{ choice_intro }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="bn-give__choice" id="bnGiveChoice">

      {%- comment -%}
        ============================================================
        THE FREE BOTTLE — the hero, and the only card on the page.
        Shopify does NOT auto-hide sold-out product pages, and URL
        redirects only fire on would-be-404s. This conditional IS the
        sold-out mechanism, and it is driven by `product.available`,
        never by the typed cap — so it survives `show_cap` being off.
        ============================================================
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if product.available -%}

        <section class="bn-give__card bn-give__card--offer" aria-labelledby="bnGiveHeading">

          {%- comment -%} Stock chip. Nothing renders here unless `show_cap` is on. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if scarcity_line != blank -%}
            <p class="bn-give__pill">{{ scarcity_line }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if hero_img != blank -%}
            <div class="bn-give__media">
              <img
                class="bn-give__hero-img"
                src="{{ hero_img | image_url: width: 720 }}"
                srcset="{{ hero_img | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ hero_img | image_url: width: 720 }} 720w, {{ hero_img | image_url: width: 1080 }} 1080w"
                sizes="(min-width: 900px) 460px, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
                width="{{ hero_img.width }}"
                height="{{ hero_img.height }}"
                alt="{{ hero_alt | escape }}"
                fetchpriority="high"
              >
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%} Dark pill, per the wireframe. {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="bn-give__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | default: 'One-time free product giveaway' }}</p>

          {%- comment -%}
            The headline IS the Free claim now — there is no separate price word.
            `| money` prints "$0.00" for a genuinely free SKU, so the claim is
            branched on the REAL price instead: if this variant is ever priced
            above zero, the page states that price and never says "free". The
            old big "Free" display type carried this same guard; it moved here
            with it. Do not collapse this back to a single unconditional line.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <h1 class="bn-give__title" id="bnGiveHeading">
            {%- if price_is_zero -%}
              <span class="bn-give__hl-line">{{ headline_line1 }}</span>
              <span class="bn-give__hl-line">{{ headline_line2 }}</span>
            {%- else -%}
              <span class="bn-give__hl-line">{{ headline_line1 }}</span>
              <span class="bn-give__hl-line">get {{ product.title }} for {{ current_variant.price | money }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </h1>

          {%- if section.settings.subhead != blank -%}
            <p class="bn-give__subhead">{{ section.settings.subhead }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            FTC 251.1(c)(1) — every condition, at the outset, in the same block
            as the Free claim, and BEFORE the Subscribe & Save module rather than
            after it (see the adjacency note in the header comment). Not a
            footnote. Not behind the FAQ. This list is the ONLY place these
            conditions are stated on this card, so a line deleted here is a
            condition disclosed nowhere.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <ul class="bn-give__terms">
            <li>{{ ship_amount }} flat shipping, paid by you</li>
            {%- comment -%} Cap bullet: `show_cap` off by default, and suppressed anyway when real inventory contradicts the typed cap. {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if cap_trusted -%}
              <li>{{ cap }} bottles total</li>
            {%- endif -%}
            <li>One per customer</li>
            <li>US shipping addresses only</li>
          </ul>

          {%- comment -%}
            16 CFR 435 — ship commitment stated separately from transit time.

            The ship-by half ("within 2 business days") is our own commitment and
            is safe to state. The transit half is a CARRIER service level: until
            Jeff confirms we are actually buying a guaranteed 2-day service, any
            "2-day transit" wording is an unverified representation under
            16 CFR 435, so it is stated only as "tracked".
            RESTORE ONLY IF a guaranteed 2-day service is confirmed in writing:
              Ships within 2 business days. Tracked 2-day transit once shipped.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="bn-give__ship">
            Ships within 2 business days. Tracked the whole way.
          </p>

          {%- comment -%}
            ============================================================
            SUBSCRIBE & SAVE — the paid option, offered before the claim.

            Renders in one of two states:
              empty  — the pitch and a "Choose" button that opens the picker
              chosen — the fragrance that is now IN THE CART, plus "Change"

            The chosen state is decided SERVER-SIDE from cart.items, not from
            sessionStorage, so the recurring-charge disclosure is on the page on
            first paint whenever a recurring line actually exists. JS moves
            between the states live; it is not what makes the disclosure appear.

            If nothing in the picker collection is subscribable, the button is
            replaced by a plain link out. A "Choose" that opens an empty sheet
            is a dead end.
            ============================================================
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="bn-give__sub" id="bnGiveSub">
            <p class="bn-give__sub-pill">{{ section.settings.option_b_heading | default: 'Subscribe & save' }}</p>

            <div class="bn-give__sub-empty" id="bnGiveSubEmpty" {% if cart_sub_line != blank %}hidden{% endif %}>
              <span class="bn-give__sub-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
              <p class="bn-give__sub-copy">
                {{ section.settings.option_b_body | default: 'Add a bottle' }}{% if sub_free_shipping %} + free shipping{% endif %} —
                <strong>first month {{ sub_first_price }}, then {{ sub_price }}</strong>
              </p>
              {%- if pick_count > 0 -%}
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="bn-give__sub-choose"
                  id="bnGiveChoose"
                  aria-haspopup="dialog"
                  aria-controls="bnGivePicker"
                >{{ section.settings.option_b_button | default: 'Choose' }}</button>
              {%- else -%}
                {%- comment -%} Nothing subscribable to show: link out rather than open an empty sheet. {%- endcomment -%}
                <a class="bn-give__sub-choose" href="{{ option_b_url }}">{{ section.settings.option_b_button | default: 'Choose' }}</a>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

            <div class="bn-give__sub-chosen" id="bnGiveSubChosen" {% if cart_sub_line == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>
              {%- if cart_sub_line != blank and cart_sub_line.image != blank -%}
                <img
                  class="bn-give__sub-thumb"
                  id="bnGiveSubThumb"
                  src="{{ cart_sub_line.image | image_url: width: 128 }}"
                  width="64"
                  height="64"
                  alt=""
                  loading="lazy"
                >
              {%- else -%}
                {%- comment -%} No src attribute at all: src="" makes some browsers re-request the page. JS sets it. {%- endcomment -%}
                <img class="bn-give__sub-thumb" id="bnGiveSubThumb" width="64" height="64" alt="" loading="lazy" hidden>
              {%- endif -%}
              <div class="bn-give__sub-chosen-text">
                <p class="bn-give__sub-title" id="bnGiveSubTitle">{{ cart_sub_line.product.title }}</p>
                <p class="bn-give__sub-terms">first month {{ sub_first_price }}, then {{ sub_price }}</p>
              </div>
              <button type="button" class="bn-give__sub-change" id="bnGiveChange">Change</button>
            </div>

            <p class="bn-give__sub-status" id="bnGiveSubStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

            {%- comment -%}
              ROSCA. Once a scent is chosen, this page IS taking a subscription
              decision, so the full auto-renewal disclosure has to be on screen —
              not a fineprint line. Hidden until then, because until then the
              page offers nothing recurring.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="bn-give__sub-disclosure" id="bnGiveSubDisclosure" {% if cart_sub_line == blank %}hidden{% endif %}>
              {% render 'subscription-renewal-disclosure', surface: 'pdp' %}
            </div>
          </div>

          {%- if customer_claimed -%}
            {%- comment -%} Customer layer: tagged `giveaway_claimed` by Flow 1 on a previous order. {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="bn-give__claimed" role="status">
              <p class="bn-give__claimed-title">You've already claimed your free 5ml — thank you.</p>
              <p class="bn-give__claimed-note">One per customer, so there is nothing more to claim here. The monthly rotation is still open to you.</p>
            </div>
          {%- elsif already_claimed -%}
            {%- comment -%} Cart layer: the bottle is sitting in this visitor's cart right now. {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="bn-give__claimed" role="status">
              <p class="bn-give__claimed-title">Your free 5ml is in your cart</p>
              <p class="bn-give__claimed-note">One per customer, so there's nothing more to add here.</p>
              <a class="bn-give__btn bn-give__btn--primary" href="{{ routes.cart_url | default: '/cart' }}">Go to cart</a>
            </div>
          {%- else -%}
          {%- form 'product', product, id: 'bnGiveForm', class: 'bn-give__form' -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ current_variant.id }}">
            {%- comment -%} Quantity is locked to 1. There is deliberately no selector. {%- endcomment -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
            {%- comment -%} Underscore-prefixed property: hidden from the customer, used by fulfilment + one-per-customer checks. {%- endcomment -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="properties[_bn_offer]" value="free-5ml">

            {%- comment -%} Label is the claim only. The shipping charge is stated once, in the terms list above. {%- endcomment -%}
            <button type="submit" class="bn-give__btn bn-give__btn--primary" id="bnGiveBtn">
              <span class="bn-give__btn-label" id="bnGiveBtnLabel">{{ claim_label }}</span>
            </button>
          {%- endform -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          <p class="bn-give__status" id="bnGiveStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

          {%- comment -%}
            Fineprint. Swaps to the recurring-charge wording the moment a
            subscription is in the cart, because "no subscription, no
            auto-renewal" stops being true at that point. Server-rendered from
            the cart, then kept in step by JS.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="bn-give__fineprint" id="bnGiveFineprint">{% if cart_sub_line != blank %}{{ fineprint_sub }}{% else %}{{ fineprint }}{% endif %}</p>

        </section>

      {%- else -%}

        <section class="bn-give__card bn-give__card--waitlist" aria-labelledby="bnGiveHeading">
          {%- liquid
            comment
              With `show_cap` off the sold-out copy must not name a batch size, so the
              headline falls back to the same neutral sentence the badge carries — and
              the badge is then suppressed rather than echoed back at the visitor.
            endcomment
            assign soldout_pill = section.settings.soldout_pill | default: 'This release is finished'
            assign waitlist_heading = section.settings.waitlist_heading
            if waitlist_heading == blank
              if show_cap
                assign waitlist_heading = 'All ' | append: cap | append: ' bottles are gone.'
              else
                assign waitlist_heading = 'This release is finished'
              endif
            endif
          -%}
          {%- if soldout_pill != blank and soldout_pill != waitlist_heading -%}
            <p class="bn-give__pill bn-give__pill--muted">{{ soldout_pill }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          <h1 class="bn-give__title" id="bnGiveHeading">{{ waitlist_heading }}</h1>
          {%- comment -%}
            TRUTHFULNESS: this is Shopify's `form 'customer'` newsletter signup.
            It marks the visitor marketing-subscribed and syncs to Klaviyo, so it
            CANNOT promise "one email only". The copy below describes what the
            form actually does. If a genuine single-send waitlist is wanted, it
            needs a non-marketing capture (metafield / Klaviyo list with no
            campaigns), not a copy change.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="bn-give__subhead">
            {{ section.settings.waitlist_body | default: "Leave your email and we'll tell you when the next batch is released. This adds you to the Base Note email list, so you'll get our other updates too. Unsubscribe from any email, any time." }}
          </p>

          {%- form 'customer', id: 'bnGiveWaitlistForm', class: 'bn-give__waitlist-form' -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="free-5ml-waitlist">
            {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
              <p class="bn-give__note bn-give__note--ok">You're on the list. We'll email you when the next batch is released.</p>
            {%- elsif form.errors -%}
              <p class="bn-give__note bn-give__note--bad">{{ form.errors.messages['email'] | default: 'That email address did not look right. Please try again.' }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            <label class="bn-give__label" for="bnGiveWaitlistEmail">Email address</label>
            <div class="bn-give__waitlist-row">
              <input
                type="email"
                id="bnGiveWaitlistEmail"
                name="contact[email]"
                class="bn-give__input"
                placeholder="you@example.com"
                autocomplete="email"
                required
              >
              <button type="submit" class="bn-give__btn bn-give__btn--primary bn-give__btn--compact">
                {{ section.settings.waitlist_button | default: 'Notify me' }}
              </button>
            </div>
          {%- endform -%}
        </section>

      {%- endif -%}

    </div>

    {%- comment -%} ===================== FAQ ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
    <section class="bn-give__faq-wrap" aria-labelledby="bnGiveFaqHeading">
      <h2 class="bn-give__faq-title" id="bnGiveFaqHeading">{{ section.settings.faq_heading | default: 'Straight answers' }}</h2>
      <div class="bn-give__faq">
        {%- assign faq_q1 = section.settings.faq_q1 | default: 'Is it really free?' -%}
        {%- assign faq_q2 = section.settings.faq_q2 | default: 'When will it arrive?' -%}
        {%- assign faq_q3 = section.settings.faq_q3 | default: 'Am I signing up for anything?' -%}
        {%- assign faq_q4 = section.settings.faq_q4 | default: 'What is a 5ml atomizer?' -%}
        {%- assign faq_q5 = section.settings.faq_q5 | default: 'One per customer?' -%}

        {%- if faq_q1 != blank -%}
          <details class="bn-give__faq-item">
            <summary>{{ faq_q1 }}</summary>
            <div class="bn-give__faq-answer">
              {%- comment -%} Figure comes from `ship_amount`, never hardcoded. See `faq_a1_default` above. {%- endcomment -%}
              {{ section.settings.faq_a1 | default: faq_a1_default }}
            </div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if faq_q2 != blank -%}
          <details class="bn-give__faq-item">
            <summary>{{ faq_q2 }}</summary>
            <div class="bn-give__faq-answer">
              {%- comment -%} 16 CFR 435: ship-by is our commitment; transit time is the carrier's and is not guaranteed. {%- endcomment -%}
              {{ section.settings.faq_a2 | default: '<p>We ship within 2 business days of your order. Once it leaves us it is tracked the whole way, and you get a tracking link by email the moment the label is created. Transit time after that is up to the carrier.</p>' }}
            </div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if faq_q3 != blank -%}
          <details class="bn-give__faq-item">
            <summary>{{ faq_q3 }}</summary>
            <div class="bn-give__faq-answer">
              {{ section.settings.faq_a3 | default: '<p>No. This is a one-time order. No subscription is created and nothing renews. If you want the monthly rotation, that is a separate offer at a separate price, linked at the top of this page.</p>' }}
            </div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if faq_q4 != blank -%}
          <details class="bn-give__faq-item">
            <summary>{{ faq_q4 }}</summary>
            <div class="bn-give__faq-answer">
              {{ section.settings.faq_a4 | default: '<p>A pocket-sized travel spray holding 5ml of the same fragrance you would find in the full-size bottle. That is roughly 60 sprays, about a month of daily wear, and it is small enough to be TSA friendly.</p>' }}
            </div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if faq_q5 != blank -%}
          <details class="bn-give__faq-item">
            <summary>{{ faq_q5 }}</summary>
            <div class="bn-give__faq-answer">
              {{ section.settings.faq_a5 | default: '<p>Yes. One per person and one per shipping address. If you are signed in and have claimed before, the button is replaced with a note. Duplicate orders are cancelled and refunded in full, including the shipping charge.</p>' }}
            </div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================
  SECOND-SCENT PICKER
  ============================================================
  Built here on purpose. `snippets/fragrance-selector.liquid` is the ACCOUNT
  swap modal: it changes the fragrance on an EXISTING Appstle contract through
  the customer portal. This one creates a NEW cart line with a selling plan for
  a visitor who may not even have an account. Same visual idea, completely
  different semantics and completely different failure modes. Do not merge them.

  Rendered only when there is something subscribable to show; the module falls
  back to a plain link otherwise, so this element and the button that opens it
  appear and disappear together.

  Rows skip: this giveaway SKU (you cannot subscribe to the free bottle) and any
  product with no selling plan (a row that cannot produce a subscription is a
  row that produces a full-price surprise).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if pick_count > 0 -%}
  <div class="bn-give-picker" id="bnGivePicker" hidden>
    <div class="bn-give-picker__backdrop" data-bn-picker-close></div>

    <div
      class="bn-give-picker__panel"
      role="dialog"
      aria-modal="true"
      aria-labelledby="bnGivePickerTitle"
    >
      <div class="bn-give-picker__head">
        <h2 class="bn-give-picker__title" id="bnGivePickerTitle">{{ picker_title }}</h2>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="bn-give-picker__close"
          id="bnGivePickerClose"
          data-bn-picker-close
          aria-label="Close"
        >&times;</button>
      </div>

      <ul class="bn-give-picker__list">
        {%- for p in pick_products limit: 60 -%}
          {%- if p.handle == product.handle -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- if p.selling_plan_groups.size == 0 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign pv = p.selected_or_first_available_variant
            assign pplan = p.selling_plan_groups[0].selling_plans[0]
          -%}
          <li class="bn-give-picker__row">
            {%- if p.featured_image != blank -%}
              <img
                class="bn-give-picker__thumb"
                src="{{ p.featured_image | image_url: width: 128 }}"
                srcset="{{ p.featured_image | image_url: width: 128 }} 128w, {{ p.featured_image | image_url: width: 256 }} 256w"
                sizes="64px"
                width="64"
                height="64"
                alt=""
                loading="lazy"
              >
            {%- else -%}
              <span class="bn-give-picker__thumb bn-give-picker__thumb--empty" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {%- endif -%}

            <div class="bn-give-picker__text">
              {%- if p.vendor != blank -%}
                <p class="bn-give-picker__vendor">{{ p.vendor }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              <p class="bn-give-picker__name">{{ p.title }}</p>
              <p class="bn-give-picker__price">first month {{ sub_first_price }} &middot; then {{ sub_price }}</p>
              <a
                class="bn-give-picker__explore"
                href="{{ p.url }}"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
              >{{ picker_explore_label }} &rarr;</a>
            </div>

            {%- comment -%}
              The plan id is read here, server-side, from the product's own
              selling plan group. It is never inferred in JS and never reused
              from another product.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="bn-give-picker__choose"
              data-bn-pick
              data-variant-id="{{ pv.id }}"
              data-selling-plan="{{ pplan.id }}"
              data-title="{{ p.title | escape }}"
              data-image="{{ p.featured_image | image_url: width: 128 }}"
              data-handle="{{ p.handle }}"
            >Choose</button>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Sticky mobile CTA. Rendered only when there is something to claim, and hidden
  by CSS until JS reveals it — so a no-JS visitor never sees a dead button.
  It is revealed only once the whole choice block has scrolled ABOVE the
  viewport, so it can never cover the button it duplicates.

  FTC 251.1(c)(1) — THIS BAR MUST BE SELF-SUFFICIENT.
  By design it appears only after the disclosure block has scrolled off-screen,
  which means it is the ONLY thing on screen making the Free claim at that
  moment, on effectively all mobile traffic. A restated Free claim carries the
  full set of conditions with it, so the conditions ride in the bar's own text:
  shipping charge, batch cap, one per customer, US only. Do not shorten this to
  a price chip. If you need the space back, remove the word "free" from the bar
  entirely — a bar that makes no Free claim needs no conditions.
  The cap clause follows the same `cap_trusted` guard as the main block, so the
  bar can never state a batch size that real inventory contradicts, and with
  `show_cap` off it is not printed at all.

  The bar is ALSO gated on `show_claim`: when the bottle is already in the cart,
  or the customer is tagged `giveaway_claimed`, the main card renders a claimed
  state with no button — but the sticky bar has its own button wired to the same
  /cart/add.js call, and /cart/add.js MERGES a matching line and ADDS the
  quantity. An ungated bar is a second doorway to a second bottle.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product.available and section.settings.show_sticky and show_claim -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign sticky_terms = 'Free bottle · ' | append: ship_amount | append: ' shipping'
    if cap_trusted
      assign sticky_terms = sticky_terms | append: ' · ' | append: cap | append: ' bottles'
    endif
    assign sticky_terms = sticky_terms | append: ' · one per customer, US only'
  -%}
  <div class="bn-give-sticky" id="bnGiveSticky" hidden>
    <div class="bn-give-sticky__inner">
      <p class="bn-give-sticky__terms">{{ sticky_terms }}</p>
      <button type="button" class="bn-give__btn bn-give__btn--primary bn-give-sticky__btn" id="bnGiveStickyBtn">
        <span id="bnGiveStickyLabel">{{ claim_label_short }}</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

<style>
  .bn-give {
    background: var(--color-background);
    padding: var(--spacing-lg) 0 var(--spacing-3xl);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bn-give__wrap {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1080px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--container-padding, 1.5rem);
  }

  /* ---------- choice block ---------- */
  .bn-give__intro {
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--spacing-md);
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* One centred column at every width. There is no second column to fall back
     to, so nothing here changes at the desktop breakpoint except the padding. */
  .bn-give__choice {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .bn-give__card {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg, 12px);
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
  }

  .bn-give__card--offer {
    border-color: var(--color-primary);
    border-width: 2px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  /* ---------- subscription strip ----------
     Quiet by construction: no card chrome, no fill, body-weight type and a text
     link. If this ever grows a background, a border and a filled button it has
     become a second offer, which is the layout Jeff rejected. */
  .bn-give__strip {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 4px 10px;
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
    padding: 0 2px 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .bn-give__strip-text {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-light);
  }

  .bn-give__strip-text strong {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bn-give__strip-link {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    min-height: 24px;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .bn-give__strip-link:hover,
  .bn-give__strip-link:focus-visible {
    color: var(--color-secondary);
  }

  /* ---------- offer head ---------- */
  .bn-give__pill {
    display: inline-block;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    padding: 5px 12px;
    background: var(--color-secondary);
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full, 9999px);
  }

  .bn-give__pill--muted {
    background: var(--color-background-secondary);
    color: var(--color-text-light);
  }

  /* Hero photo: full bottle beside the 5 ml atomizer. Wide, not a thumbnail. */
  .bn-give__media {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    background: var(--color-background-secondary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 8px);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .bn-give__hero-img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  /* Dark pill, per the wireframe. */
  .bn-give__eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    padding: 9px 18px;
    background: var(--color-primary);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: {{ section.settings.eyebrow_size | default: 12 }}px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full, 9999px);
  }

  .bn-give__title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: {{ section.settings.headline_size_mobile | default: 30 }}px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin: 0;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* Two lines: the charge, then what it buys. The second is lighter so the
     price lands first, which is the order the wireframe reads in. */
  .bn-give__hl-line { display: block; }

  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .bn-give__title { font-size: {{ section.settings.headline_size_desktop | default: 36 }}px; }
  }

  .bn-give__hl-line + .bn-give__hl-line {
    margin-top: 2px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bn-give__subhead {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-light);
  }

  /* ---------- price ---------- */
  .bn-give__price {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 10px 0 0;
  }

  .bn-give__price-word {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 46px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  /* ---------- FTC conditions, at the outset ---------- */
  .bn-give__terms {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 4px 14px;
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .bn-give__terms li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 15px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bn-give__terms li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 7px;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-secondary);
  }

  .bn-give__ship {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-text-light);
  }

  /* ---------- buttons ---------- */
  .bn-give__form {
    margin: 14px 0 0;
  }

  .bn-give__btn {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 52px;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    /* Option 1's CTA is an <a>, so the reset has to live on the shared class. */
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm, 4px);
    border: 2px solid transparent;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.2s, color 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
  }

  .bn-give__btn--primary {
    background: var(--color-primary);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .bn-give__btn--primary:hover,
  .bn-give__btn--primary:focus-visible {
    background: var(--color-text);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .bn-give__btn--primary[disabled],
  .bn-give__btn--primary.is-busy {
    opacity: 0.7;
    cursor: progress;
  }

  .bn-give__btn--ghost {
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    border-color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .bn-give__btn--ghost:hover,
  .bn-give__btn--ghost:focus-visible {
    background: var(--color-primary);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .bn-give__btn--compact {
    width: auto;
    min-width: 128px;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }

  /* ---------- Subscribe & save module ---------- */
  .bn-give__sub {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    padding: 14px;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 8px);
  }

  .bn-give__sub-pill {
    display: inline-block;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    padding: 5px 12px;
    background: var(--color-secondary);
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full, 9999px);
  }

  .bn-give__sub-empty,
  .bn-give__sub-chosen {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .bn-give__sub-empty[hidden],
  .bn-give__sub-chosen[hidden],
  .bn-give__sub-disclosure[hidden] { display: none; }

  .bn-give__sub-plus {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-dark, #D5D3D0);
    border-radius: 50%;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .bn-give__sub-copy {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .bn-give__sub-copy strong { font-weight: 700; }

  /* Text button: the claim below is the page's only filled CTA. */
  .bn-give__sub-choose,
  .bn-give__sub-change {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 10px 4px;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .bn-give__sub-choose:hover,
  .bn-give__sub-choose:focus-visible,
  .bn-give__sub-change:hover,
  .bn-give__sub-change:focus-visible { color: var(--color-secondary); }

  .bn-give__sub-thumb {
    flex: 0 0 48px;
